<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Disabled is asserted; output is OFF; feedback Status shown if available; Alarms disabled]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OFF-SCAN (EnableIn is False) STATUS
============================================================
If this device is OFF-SCAN (rung is false or EnableIn is false in FBD), then:

Handle "NO MODE" Selection using the standard P_Mode AOI (EnableInFalse Routine, false scan required!).

NOTE:  IN ORDER TO AVOID USING AN "AFI" (which will generate a routine verify warning),
THIS RUNG USES AN XIC of Cfg_PCmdClear, followed by an XIO of the SAME BIT
to ensure P_Mode is SCANNED FALSE ("NO MODE").

THIS IS NOT DEAD CODE AND MUST APPEAR EXACTLY AS SHOWN FOR PROPER OPERATION!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)XIO(Cfg_PCmdClear)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration still needs to happen, even when device is disabled.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTU(PCmd_Off)OTU(PCmd_On)OTU(PCmd_OnPulse)OTU(PCmd_OffPulse)OTU(PCmd_ContPulse);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_On) OTU(OCmd_Off) OTU(OCmd_OnPulse) OTU(OCmd_OffPulse) ,OTU(OCmd_ContPulse) OTU(OCmd_Bypass) OTU(OCmd_Check) OTU(MCmd_Disable) ,OTU(MCmd_Enable) OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Override Command is set to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[ 
Since we're not processing Operator Commands or Settings, we're not READY for any of them either!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Rdy_On) OTU(Rdy_Off) OTU(Rdy_OnPulse) OTU(Rdy_OffPulse) ,OTU(Rdy_ContPulse) OTU(Rdy_Bypass) OTU(Rdy_Check) OTU(Rdy_Disable) ,OTU(Rdy_Enable) OTU(Rdy_Reset) OTU(Rdy_ResetAckAll) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
FEEDBACK DETERMINATION
============================================================
If the Device is being simulated or has no feedbacks, use the Sim Timers to provide
"fake" feedback signals based on the simulation time to turn ON and OFF the device.

If the Device is NOT being simulated and it HAS and IS USING feedback,
interpret the state of the configured feedbacks to determint the Device state..]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)[XIC(Cfg_UseOnFdbk) XIC(Inp_OnFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_UseOnFdbk) XIC(Cfg_UseOffFdbk) XIO(Inp_OffFdbk) ]OTE(Wrk_OnFdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Device is being simulated or has no feedbacks, use the Sim Timers to provide
"fake" feedback signals based on the simulation time to turn ON and OFF the device.

If the Device is NOT being simulated and it HAS and IS USING feedback,
interpret the state of the configured feedbacks to determint the Device state..]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Inp_Sim) ,XIO(Cfg_UseOffFdbk) XIO(Cfg_UseOnFdbk) ] ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Cfg_UseOffFdbk) XIC(Inp_OffFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_UseOffFdbk) XIC(Cfg_UseOnFdbk) XIO(Inp_OnFdbk) ] ]OTE(Wrk_OffFdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Wrk_OnFdbk) XIC(Wrk_OffFdbk) MOV(1,Val_Fdbk) OTE(Sts_FdbkOff) ,XIC(Wrk_OnFdbk) XIO(Wrk_OffFdbk) MOV(2,Val_Fdbk) OTE(Sts_FdbkOn) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Device can be configured to have Feedbakc Failure shown for both
feedback inputs ON or for both inputs OFF.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_FdbkFail) XIC(Wrk_OnFdbk) XIC(Wrk_OffFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_FdbkFail) XIO(Wrk_OnFdbk) XIO(Wrk_OffFdbk) ]OTE(Sts_FdbkFail)MOV(3,Val_Fdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The OTHER (non-failure) state with both feedback inputs ON or both inputs OFF is
DEVICE IN TRANSIT.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_FdbkFail) XIO(Wrk_OnFdbk) XIO(Wrk_OffFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_FdbkFail) XIC(Wrk_OnFdbk) XIC(Wrk_OffFdbk) ]CLR(Val_Fdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset the output pulse, fault, and simulation timers.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[RES(Wrk_OnT) RES(Wrk_OffT) RES(Wrk_OnDelayT) RES(Wrk_OffDelayT) ,RES(Wrk_OnPulseT) RES(Wrk_OffPulseT) RES(Wrk_SimOnT) RES(Wrk_SimOffT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Discrete Output is DE-ENERGIZED]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Sts_Out)OTU(Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Show the device as Disabled and Not Ready, not Available, and with no
Maintenance Bypass breadcrumb.
Show the status of the output bit as DE-ENERGIZED.
Show the enumerated device command as NONE.
Show the enumerated device status as DISABLED.
Show the enumerated internal state as DE-ENERGIZED.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTL(Sts_Disabled) OTU(Sts_Available) OTU(Sts_MaintByp) OTL(Sts_NotRdy) ,OTL(Nrdy_NoMode) OTU(Nrdy_Disabled) OTU(Nrdy_CfgErr) OTU(Nrdy_Intlk) ,OTU(Nrdy_Perm) OTU(Nrdy_OperPrio) OTU(Nrdy_Fail) OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ,CLR(Val_Cmd) MOV(33,Val_Sts) CLR(Val_State) CLR(Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED SOURCE / QUALITY VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality for Input / Output values / status (SrcQ_IO)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MOV(20,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(20,SrcQ);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Alarms are turned off when off-scan, so clear the Notification Level.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Alm_OnFail) OTU(Alm_OffFail) OTU(Alm_IntlkTrip) OTU(Alm_IOFault) ,OTU(Sts_OnFail) OTU(Sts_OffFail) OTU(Sts_IntlkTrip) OTU(Sts_IOFault) ,OTL(Sts_AlmInh) CLR(Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Control Discrete Output, monitoring Feedbacks]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_DOut:  PROCESS -- DISCRETE OUTPUT (on/off device)
============================================================
Revision 3.1-02 Release  2014-09-30:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib. Uses P_Alarm V3.0, P_Mode V3.0.
Added Cfg_OperOffPrio.  Complex rung split apart for
proper operation on RSLogix Emualte 5000.
V3.0-01  2013-07-30:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-02  2013-09-03:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-03  2013-10-30:  Corrected Parameter descriptions and default
configuration values for alarms only.
V3.0-04  2014-06-12:  Fixed I/O Fault Ready to Reset logic.
V3.1-00  2014-07-08:  Modified to use P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1;
added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_Xxxxx), source/quality values (SrcQ).
Modified to consistently use alias tag names.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Exposed Pulse, Delay and Fault timers ACC/PRE read-only.
Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic. Using P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1-01.
V3.1-02  2014-09-30:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-02.
============================================================
This Instruction controls (and optionally monitors feedback for)
a single Discrete Output and provides:

*  Operator and Program Commands to:
    -  turn the output ON
    -  turn the output OFF
    -  if the output is OFF, pulse it ON for a configured time
    -  if the output is ON, pulse it OFF for a configured time, or
    -  pulse the output continuously at the configured ON
        and OFF times (e.g., for blinking a lamp)
*  User-configurable ON delay and OFF delay before first output change
*  User-configurable text labels for the ON and OFF states
*  Optional monitoring of ON and OFF state confirmation feedbacks
*  Detection of Failure to turn ON or OFF (when feedbacks are used)
*  Monitoring of Permissive conditions to allow energizing output
*  Monitoring of Interlock conditions to de-energize output
*  Optional return to previous state upon return from Hand Mode,
      Override Mode or Interlock
*  Simulation, providing feedback of a working device while
      disabling output (keeping de-energized)
*  Monitoring of I/O communication faults
*  Alarms for Fail to Turn ON, Fail to turn OFF (if feedbacks are
      used), Interlock Trip, I/O Fault
*  "Available" status for use by automation logic to know whether
      output can be controlled by other objects.

Modes are provided by a P_Mode AOI instance.
Alarms are provided by P_Alarm AOI instances.
Modes of operation: Operator, Program, Override, Maintenance, Hand
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag)LOWER(Cfg_0StText,Cfg_1StText)LOWER(Inf_Lib,Inf_Type);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MODE PROCESSING
============================================================
This rung handles received Mode Inputs and Commands:

NOTE:  All Commands for Mode, Alarm are aliased directly to the
corresponding Commands in the contained P_Mode and P_Alarm AOIs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles simple First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONFIGURATION
============================================================
If the device does not even HAVE Feedback inputs,
they cannot be USED for feedback checking!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasOnFdbk) OTU(Cfg_UseOnFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_HasOffFdbk) OTU(Cfg_UseOffFdbk) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These rungs get Configuration data (such as timer presets) and distribute as needed.
Note that some Configuration data are used directly in-place.

Enter the time (in seconds) for the device to successfully turn ON before declaring a fault.
Enter the time (in seconds) for the device to successfully turn OFF before declaring a fault.

If the timer preset calcuated wraps negative (more than 2.14... million seconds), then use a default
limit value and report Bad Configuration.  Note that a negative timer preset will fault the controller!!!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MUL(Cfg_OnDelayT,1000,Wrk_OnDelayT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_OnDelayT.PRE.31) MOV(0,Wrk_OnDelayT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_OffDelayT,1000,Wrk_OffDelayT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_OffDelayT.PRE.31) MOV(0,Wrk_OffDelayT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_OnPulseT,1000,Wrk_OnPulseT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_OnPulseT.PRE.31) MOV(2147483647,Wrk_OnPulseT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_OffPulseT,1000,Wrk_OffPulseT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_OffPulseT.PRE.31) MOV(2147483647,Wrk_OffPulseT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_OnFailT,1000,Wrk_OnT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_OnT.PRE.31) MOV(2147483647,Wrk_OnT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_OffFailT,1000,Wrk_OffT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_OffT.PRE.31) MOV(2147483647,Wrk_OffT.PRE) ]OTE(Err_Timer);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Enter the time (in seconds) to echo back the desired state when running in simulation

Handle timer preset invalid values as above.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MUL(Cfg_SimFdbkT,1000,Wrk_SimOnT.PRE)[XIC(Wrk_SimOnT.PRE.31) MOV(0,Wrk_SimOnT.PRE) OTE(Err_Sim) ,MOV(Wrk_SimOnT.PRE,Wrk_SimOffT.PRE) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung generates a summary Bad Config status, simply an OR of the individual bits provided above
(in the Configuration handling section).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Err_Timer) ,XIC(Err_Sim) ,[XIC(OnFail.Sts_Err) ,XIC(OffFail.Sts_Err) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Sts_Err) ,XIC(IOFault.Sts_Err) ] OTE(Err_Alarm) ]OTE(Sts_Err);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
FEEDBACK DETERMINATION
============================================================
If the Device is being simulated or has no feedbacks, use the Sim Timers to provide
"fake" feedback signals based on the simulation time to turn ON and OFF the device.

If the Device is NOT being simulated and it HAS and IS USING feedback,
interpret the state of the configured feedbacks to determint the Device state..]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Inp_Sim) ,XIO(Cfg_UseOnFdbk) XIO(Cfg_UseOffFdbk) ] [XIC(Wrk_SimOnDN) XIC(Cfg_FdbkFail) ,XIO(Wrk_SimOffDN) XIO(Cfg_FdbkFail) ] ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Cfg_UseOnFdbk) XIC(Inp_OnFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_UseOnFdbk) XIC(Cfg_UseOffFdbk) XIO(Inp_OffFdbk) ] ]OTE(Wrk_OnFdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Device is being simulated or has no feedbacks, use the Sim Timers to provide
"fake" feedback signals based on the simulation time to turn ON and OFF the device.

If the Device is NOT being simulated and it HAS and IS USING feedback,
interpret the state of the configured feedbacks to determint the Device state..]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Inp_Sim) ,XIO(Cfg_UseOffFdbk) XIO(Cfg_UseOnFdbk) ] [XIC(Wrk_SimOffDN) XIC(Cfg_FdbkFail) ,XIO(Wrk_SimOnDN) XIO(Cfg_FdbkFail) ] ,XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Cfg_UseOffFdbk) XIC(Inp_OffFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_UseOffFdbk) XIC(Cfg_UseOnFdbk) XIO(Inp_OnFdbk) ] ]OTE(Wrk_OffFdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Wrk_OnFdbk) XIC(Wrk_OffFdbk) OTE(Sts_FdbkOff) ,XIC(Wrk_OnFdbk) XIO(Wrk_OffFdbk) OTE(Sts_FdbkOn) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Device can be configured to have Feedbakc Failure shown for both
feedback inputs ON or for both inputs OFF.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_FdbkFail) XIC(Wrk_OnFdbk) XIC(Wrk_OffFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_FdbkFail) XIO(Wrk_OnFdbk) XIO(Wrk_OffFdbk) ]OTE(Sts_FdbkFail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The OTHER (non-failure) state with both feedback inputs ON or both inputs OFF is
DEVICE IN TRANSIT.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_FdbkFail) XIO(Wrk_OnFdbk) XIO(Wrk_OffFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_FdbkFail) XIC(Wrk_OnFdbk) XIC(Wrk_OffFdbk) ]CLR(Val_Fdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Sts_FdbkOff) MOV(1,Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Sts_FdbkOn) MOV(2,Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Sts_FdbkFail) MOV(3,Val_Fdbk) ] ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(4,Val_Fdbk) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
INTERLOCK / PERMISSIVE BYPASS / CHECK COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Bypass Command bypasses the Bypassable Permissives and Interlocks.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OCmd_Bypass)OTU(OCmd_Bypass)OTL(Wrk_Bypass);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Check Command enables checking of ALL
Permissives and Interlocks (cancels the bypass).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OCmd_Check)OTU(OCmd_Check)OTU(Wrk_Bypass);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the internal Bypass flag is set, Bypassable Interlocks and Permissives ARE BYPASSED.
Bypassing is ACTIVE if Bypass selected OR in Maintenance Mode,
or in Override Mode if Override Bypassing is configured.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Sts_Bypass) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Sts_Ovrd) XIC(Cfg_OvrdPermIntlk) ]OTE(Sts_BypActive);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Maintenance Bypass function is active, display the Maintenance Bypass
Indicator (triangle symbol) on the graphic symbol.  Bypass functions are:
*  Interlock / Permissive Bypass function is enabled
* Device HAS OFF or ON feedback designated by engineer, but
maintenance has selected to NOT USE that feedback]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_HasOnFdbk) XIO(Cfg_UseOnFdbk) ,XIC(Cfg_HasOffFdbk) XIO(Cfg_UseOffFdbk) ,XIC(Sts_Bypass) ]OTE(Sts_MaintByp);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready for Interlock / Permissive Bypass if not bypassed.
Ready to cancel Bypass (resume checking) if bypassed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Rdy_Bypass) ,XIC(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Rdy_Check) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE DISABLE/ENABLE COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Disable Command disables the Analog Output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_Disable)OTU(MCmd_Disable)XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)OTL(Wrk_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Enable Command cancels the Disable and enables the Analog Output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_Enable)OTU(MCmd_Enable)XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)OTU(Wrk_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the internal Disabled flag is set, the Drive is DISABLED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Disabled)OTE(Sts_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready to Disable device if in Maintenance Mode and device is NOT Disabled.
Ready to Enable device if in Maintenance Mode and device IS Disabled.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)[XIO(Wrk_Disabled) OTE(Rdy_Disable) ,XIC(Wrk_Disabled) OTE(Rdy_Enable) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM AND DEVICE RESET COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The rungs in this section handle commands for this Device, received
in Operator, Program, Override and Maintenance Modes.
(Hand mode is handled separately, below.

For any command which involves energizing the device (all commands
except OFF), permissives must be OK to energize.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Inp_PermOK) ,XIC(Sts_BypActive) ]XIC(Inp_NBPermOK)OTE(Wrk_PermOK);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM RESET COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
This rung handles the Alarm Reset Input and Commands
and the "Reset and Ack All" Operator Command.

This rung processes received Reset Commands from:

1.  The Operator via HMI Operator Command, or
2.  Higher-level strategies via Program Command
3.  Pushbuttons or other block via Input
4.  Resets initiated by other device Operator Commands (if configured to do so)

and forwards the Reset to ALL Alarms and latched Shed conditions.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_Reset) ,[XIC(OCmd_Off) ,[XIC(OCmd_On) ,XIC(OCmd_OffPulse) ,XIC(OCmd_OnPulse) ,XIC(OCmd_ContPulse) ] XIC(Wrk_PermOK) ] XIC(Cfg_OCmdResets) XIO(Sts_Err) XIO(Sts_Disabled) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) [OTL(PCmd_OnFailAck) ,OTL(PCmd_OffFailAck) ,OTL(PCmd_IntlkTripAck) ,OTL(PCmd_IOFaultAck) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Reset) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(Inp_Reset) ][OTL(OnFail.PCmd_Reset) ,OTL(OffFail.PCmd_Reset) ,OTL(IntlkTrip.PCmd_Reset) ,OTL(IOFault.PCmd_Reset) ,XIC(Sts_OnFail) RES(Wrk_OnT) ,XIC(Sts_OffFail) RES(Wrk_OffT) ,OTU(Nrdy_OperPrio) OTU(Nrdy_Fail) ,[XIO(Inp_IOFault) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ] OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
If a Device OFF command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override State is OFF,
mark the Device Target State as OFF (0).

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Cfg_OperOffPrio  #####
#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Off) OTU(OCmd_Off) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Cfg_OperOffPrio) XIO(Sts_Oper) XIO(Sts_Maint) OTL(Nrdy_OperPrio) ] ,[XIC(PCmd_Off) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Off) ,NOP() ] ,XIO(Cfg_PCmdClear) XIO(PCmd_On) XIO(PCmd_ContPulse) ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,1) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ]NEQ(Val_Sts,0)MOV(1,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Device ON command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override State is ON,
mark the Device Target State as ON (1).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_On) OTU(OCmd_On) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,[XIC(PCmd_On) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_On) ,NOP() ] ,XIO(Cfg_PCmdClear) XIC(PCmd_On) XIO(PCmd_ContPulse) ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,2) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ]XIC(Wrk_PermOK)NEQ(Val_Sts,1)MOV(2,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Device OFF PULSE command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override State is OFF PULSE,
mark the Device Target State as OFF PULSE (3).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_OffPulse) OTU(OCmd_OffPulse) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_OffPulse) OTU(PCmd_OffPulse) XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,3) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ]XIC(Wrk_PermOK)NEQ(Val_Sts,2)NEQ(Val_Sts,0)MOV(3,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Device ON PULSE command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override State is ON PULSE,
mark the Device Target State as ON PULSE (2).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_OnPulse) OTU(OCmd_OnPulse) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_OnPulse) OTU(PCmd_OnPulse) XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,4) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ]XIC(Wrk_PermOK)NEQ(Val_Sts,3)NEQ(Val_Sts,1)MOV(4,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Device CONTINUOUS PULSE command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override State is CONTINUOUSE PULSE,
mark the Device Target State as CONTINUOUS PULSE (4).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_ContPulse) OTU(OCmd_ContPulse) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_ContPulse) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_ContPulse) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,5) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ]XIC(Wrk_PermOK)NEQ(Val_Sts,4)MOV(5,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Higher Priority: HAND mode wins over others:
If in Hand, have the Device follow the feedback.
If the Device is ON, set the Target State to ON, and if the Device
is OFF, set the Target State to OFF; upon transition out of Hand, the
device will hold its last state.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_Hand) ,XIC(S:FS) ]CLR(Wrk_Cmd)[NEQ(Val_Fdbk,2) CLR(Val_Sts) CLR(Val_State) ,EQU(Val_Fdbk,2) MOV(1,Val_Sts) MOV(1,Val_State) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE FAIL TO TURN ON DETECTION
============================================================
If the DEVICE SHOULD BE ON, run an "On" Timer to check for Fail to Turn On,
and run a Simulation Timer to provide simulated ON feedback if needed.

If the ON Timer times out and the device feedback (or simulated feedback) never showed up,
show the device as "FAILED TO TURN ON" and issue an Alarm.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_OnT.DN)NEQ(Wrk_OnT.PRE,0)NEQ(Val_Fdbk,2)XIO(Sts_Maint)OTE(Sts_OnFail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE FAIL TO TURN OFF DETECTION
============================================================
If the Device SHOULD BE OFF, run an OFF Timer to check for Fail to Trun OFF,
and run a Simulation Timer to provide simulated OFF feedback if needed.

If the OFF Timer times out and the device OFF feedback (or simulated feedback) never showed "Off",
show the device as "FAILED TO TURN OFF" and issue an Alarm.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_OffT.DN)NEQ(Wrk_OffT.PRE,0)NEQ(Val_Fdbk,1)XIO(Sts_Maint)OTE(Sts_OffFail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Higher Priority:
If Interlocks are not OK (Non-Bypassable not OK, or bypassable not OK
and not bypassed by Maintenance, Override or Bypass Command), 
OR if the Device is DISABLED or FAULTED, set it to its FAIL STATE.

If the Device is NOT in its fail state (if it is energized) and the Interlock
de-energized it, raise the Interlock Trip alarm.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Rung split up for proper operation in RSLogix Emulate 5000  #####
#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Nrdy_NoMode)[XIC(Sts_Disabled) OTE(Nrdy_Disabled) ,XIC(Sts_Err) OTE(Nrdy_CfgErr) ,XIO(Wrk_PermOK) XIO(Val_State.0) OTE(Nrdy_Perm) ,[XIO(Inp_IntlkOK) XIO(Sts_BypActive) ,XIO(Inp_NBIntlkOK) ] [NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,1) NEQ(Val_Sts,0) OTE(Sts_IntlkTrip) ,OTE(Nrdy_Intlk) ] ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Sts_IOFault) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnIOFault) OTL(Nrdy_IOFault) ,XIC(Sts_OnFail) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnFail) OTL(Nrdy_Fail) ][[NEQ(Val_Sts,0) ,GRT(Wrk_Cmd,1) ] MOV(1,Wrk_Cmd) ,NOP() ]OTE(Wrk_NotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Higher Priority:
If Interlocks are not OK (Non-Bypassable not OK, or bypassable not OK
and not bypassed by Maintenance, Override or Bypass Command), 
OR if the Device is DISABLED or FAULTED, set it to its FAIL STATE.

If the Device is NOT in its fail state (if it is energized) and the Interlock
de-energized it, raise the Interlock Trip alarm.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Rung split up for proper operation in RSLogix Emulate 5000  #####
#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_NotRdy) ,XIC(Nrdy_OperPrio) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) ]OTE(Sts_NotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the device isn't "not ready" (it IS ready) and it's in Program Mode,
then it is AVAILABLE to be controlled by automation (Program Mode logic).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Prog)XIO(Sts_NotRdy)OTE(Sts_Available);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE COMMAND ENUMERATED VALUE
============================================================
Wrk_Cmd is the command currently being processed:
0 = None
1 = State 0
2 = State 1
3 = State 2
4 = State 3]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Wrk_Cmd,Val_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
STATE MACHINE
============================================================
The Discrete Output is processed using a State Machine to handle pulsing
delays, On and Off delays, commands for changes of state, etc.

These rungs handle changes of Actual State based on Target State
set by Commands above.  (Timers and the time-based
transitions follow...)

See the Timing Diagrams and state tables in the Reference
Manual for details on the state machine.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_Cmd,1)[[EQU(Val_State,1) ,EQU(Val_State,5) ,EQU(Val_State,9) ,XIO(Cfg_CompletePulse) [EQU(Val_State,7) ,EQU(Val_State,13) ] ] MOV(3,Val_State) ,[EQU(Val_State,2) ,EQU(Val_State,6) ,EQU(Val_State,10) ,EQU(Val_State,12) ,XIO(Cfg_CompletePulse) [EQU(Val_State,4) ,EQU(Val_State,8) ] ] MOV(0,Val_State) ,XIC(Cfg_CompletePulse) EQU(Val_State,8) MOV(4,Val_State) ,EQU(Val_State,11) MOV(13,Val_State) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_Cmd,2)[[EQU(Val_State,0) ,EQU(Val_State,4) ,EQU(Val_State,8) ,XIO(Cfg_CompletePulse) [EQU(Val_State,6) ,EQU(Val_State,12) ] ] MOV(2,Val_State) ,[EQU(Val_State,3) ,EQU(Val_State,7) ,EQU(Val_State,11) ,EQU(Val_State,13) ,XIO(Cfg_CompletePulse) [EQU(Val_State,5) ,EQU(Val_State,9) ] ] MOV(1,Val_State) ,XIC(Cfg_CompletePulse) EQU(Val_State,9) MOV(5,Val_State) ,EQU(Val_State,10) MOV(12,Val_State) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_Cmd,3)[XIO(Val_State.0) NEQ(Val_State,6) MOV(6,Val_State) ,XIC(Val_State.0) NEQ(Val_State,5) MOV(5,Val_State) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_Cmd,4)[XIO(Val_State.0) NEQ(Val_State,4) MOV(4,Val_State) ,XIC(Val_State.0) NEQ(Val_State,7) MOV(7,Val_State) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_Cmd,5)[[EQU(Val_State,0) ,EQU(Val_State,2) ,EQU(Val_State,4) ] MOV(8,Val_State) ,[EQU(Val_State,1) ,EQU(Val_State,3) ,EQU(Val_State,5) ] MOV(8,Val_State) ,EQU(Val_State,12) MOV(10,Val_State) ,EQU(Val_State,13) MOV(11,Val_State) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
STATE TIMERS
============================================================
Run OnDelay, OffDelay, OnPulse and OffPulse Timers in the
appropriate steps.

@@@@@  Each TON is doubled to ensure it sets or clears the  @@@@@
@@@@@  .DN bit the same scan if the timer preset is zero.  @@@@@]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GEQ(Val_State,2)[XIO(Val_State.0) [TON(Wrk_OnDelayT,?,?) TON(Wrk_OnDelayT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_OnDelayT.DN) OTE(Wrk_OnDelayDN) ,TON(Wrk_OffPulseT,?,?) TON(Wrk_OffPulseT,?,?) ] ,XIC(Val_State.0) [TON(Wrk_OffDelayT,?,?) TON(Wrk_OffDelayT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_OffDelayT.DN) OTE(Wrk_OffDelayDN) ,TON(Wrk_OnPulseT,?,?) TON(Wrk_OnPulseT,?,?) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="42" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
TIMED TRANSITIONS
============================================================
These rungs handle state transitions that are based on State Timers
(on-delay, off-delay and pulse timers) going DONE.

See the timing diagrams in the reference manual for details on these transitions.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_Cmd,1)[XIC(Wrk_OffDelayDN) EQU(Val_State,3) MOV(0,Val_State) ,XIC(Wrk_OnDelayDN) EQU(Val_State,4) MOV(7,Val_State) ,XIC(Wrk_OnPulseT.DN) [EQU(Val_State,7) ,EQU(Val_State,13) ] MOV(0,Val_State) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="43" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_Cmd,2)[XIC(Wrk_OnDelayDN) EQU(Val_State,2) MOV(1,Val_State) ,XIC(Wrk_OffDelayDN) EQU(Val_State,5) MOV(6,Val_State) ,XIC(Wrk_OffPulseT.DN) [EQU(Val_State,6) ,EQU(Val_State,12) ] MOV(1,Val_State) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="44" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_Cmd,3)[XIC(Wrk_OffDelayDN) EQU(Val_State,5) MOV(6,Val_State) ,XIC(Wrk_OffPulseT.DN) EQU(Val_State,6) MOV(1,Val_State) MOV(2,Wrk_Cmd) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="45" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_Cmd,4)[XIC(Wrk_OnDelayDN) EQU(Val_State,4) MOV(7,Val_State) ,XIC(Wrk_OnPulseT.DN) EQU(Val_State,7) MOV(0,Val_State) MOV(1,Wrk_Cmd) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="46" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_Cmd,5)[[XIC(Wrk_OnDelayDN) EQU(Val_State,8) ,XIC(Wrk_OffPulseT.DN) EQU(Val_State,10) ] MOV(11,Val_State) ,[XIC(Wrk_OffDelayDN) EQU(Val_State,9) ,XIC(Wrk_OnPulseT.DN) EQU(Val_State,11) ] MOV(10,Val_State) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="47" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the current Command if the DOut reaches a terminal state (OFF or ON).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(Val_State,0) EQU(Val_Fdbk,1) CLR(Wrk_Cmd) ,EQU(Val_State,1) EQU(Val_Fdbk,2) CLR(Wrk_Cmd) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="48" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OUTPUT GENERATION
============================================================
If the Device is NOT SIMULATED, generate the appropriate output.
From the design of the State Machine, all ODD Actual States have the
output ENERGIZED.  So just copy the least significant bit out!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Val_State.0)[XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Out) ,OTE(Sts_Out) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="49" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SIMULATION AND FAIL TIMERS
============================================================
These rungs have the timers that are based on the determined output state.

This rung has the OFF state timers.

@@@@@  Each TON that is doubled ensures it sets or clears the  @@@@@
@@@@@  .DN bit the same scan if the timer preset is zero.  @@@@@]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Sts_Out)[TON(Wrk_OffT,?,?) ,TON(Wrk_SimOffT,?,?) TON(Wrk_SimOffT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_SimOffT.DN) OTE(Wrk_SimOffDN) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="50" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[And this rung has the ON State timers.

@@@@@  Each TON that is doubled ensures it sets or clears the  @@@@@
@@@@@  .DN bit the same scan if the timer preset is zero.  @@@@@]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Out)[TON(Wrk_OnT,?,?) ,TON(Wrk_SimOnT,?,?) TON(Wrk_SimOnT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_SimOnT.DN) OTE(Wrk_SimOnDN) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="51" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
REMAINING DEVICE STATUS
============================================================
This device is PULSING if any of the Pulse commands has been issued
(and, for single pulses, not completed):
ON PULSE, OFF PULSE or CONTINUOUS PULSE]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(Val_Cmd,3) ,EQU(Val_Cmd,4) ,EQU(Val_Cmd,5) ]OTE(Sts_Pulsing);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="52" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Val_Sts is the current device status, as determined by this AOI,
based on its knowledge of commands executed and feedback.
(This is the status that should be monitored by, for example, FT Historian.)
0 = Off
1 = On
2 = Pulse Off
3 = Pulse On
4 = Pulse Continuous
5 = Turning On
6 = Turning Off
33 = Device Disabled]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Sts_Hand)[EQU(Wrk_Cmd,0) EQU(Val_State,0) CLR(Val_Sts) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,0) EQU(Val_State,1) MOV(1,Val_Sts) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,3) MOV(2,Val_Sts) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,4) MOV(3,Val_Sts) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,5) MOV(4,Val_Sts) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,1) MOV(5,Val_Sts) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,2) MOV(6,Val_Sts) ,XIC(Wrk_Disabled) MOV(33,Val_Sts) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="53" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Val_Fault is the current device fault status, as determined by this AOI,
based on its knowledge of commands executed and feedback.
(This is the fault status that should be monitored by, for example, FT Historian.)
0 = None
16 = Feedback Fault
32 = I/O Fault (from Input)
34 = Configuration Error]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Fault) ,[XIC(Sts_OnFail) ,XIC(Sts_OffFail) ] MOV(16,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) XIO(Inp_Sim) MOV(32,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_Err) MOV(34,Wrk_Fault) ,MOV(Wrk_Fault,Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="54" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED SOURCE / QUALITY VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality for Input / Output values / status (SrcQ_IO)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(9,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="55" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(SrcQ_IO,SrcQ);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="56" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OPERATOR COMMAND READIES
============================================================

Ready to TURN OFF if in Operator Manual, NOT in the OFF target state, and Interlocks are OK.
Ready to TURN ON if in Operator or Maintenancel, NOT in the ON target state, and Interlocks and permissives are OK.

Similar logic applies to the PULSE ON, PULSE OFF and CONTINUOUS PULSE readies.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Cfg_OperOffPrio  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_NotRdy)[XIO(Sts_NotRdy) ,XIC(Cfg_OCmdResets) ][[XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Cfg_OperOffPrio) ] NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,1) NEQ(Val_Sts,0) OTE(Rdy_Off) ,[XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] XIC(Wrk_PermOK) [NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,2) NEQ(Val_Sts,1) OTE(Rdy_On) ,NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,3) NEQ(Val_Sts,2) NEQ(Val_Sts,0) OTE(Rdy_OffPulse) ,NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,4) NEQ(Val_Sts,3) NEQ(Val_Sts,1) OTE(Rdy_OnPulse) ,NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,5) NEQ(Val_Sts,4) OTE(Rdy_ContPulse) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="57" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM PROCESSING
============================================================
Pass the Cfg_PCmdClear configuration down to each P_Alarm instance.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(OnFail.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(OffFail.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(IntlkTrip.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(IOFault.Cfg_PCmdClear);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="58" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The various alarms are ALWAYS allowed to Exist (Cfg_HasXxxAlarm can be 1), EXCEPT:
* If the device DOES NOT HAVE ANY FEEDBACKS, the On Fail and Off Fail
alarms will never occur and should not exist.  (If either feedback exists, 
the Fail alarm must be allowed to exist.)

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added PCfg_AllowExist on P_Alarm 3.0.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTL(IntlkTrip.PCfg_AllowExist) OTL(IOFault.PCfg_AllowExist) ,[XIC(Cfg_HasOnFdbk) ,XIC(Cfg_HasOffFdbk) ] OTE(OnFail.PCfg_AllowExist) OTE(OffFail.PCfg_AllowExist) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="59" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Failed to Confirm Output ON Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(OnFail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="60" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Failed to Confirm Output OFF Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(OffFail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="61" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Interlock Trip Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(IntlkTrip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="62" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle I/O Fault Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(IOFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="63" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If ANY alarm is Disabled, Inhibited or Suppressed, set the Alarm Inhibit
summary status bit (which puts the "I" box on the graphic symbol).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OnFail.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(OffFail.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(IOFault.Sts_AlmInh) ]OTE(Sts_AlmInh);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="64" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
NOTIFICATION VALUE
============================================================
Indicate the current alarm notification level as the max of any of the alarms,
and set the low-order bit for reset or ack required:
0 = Not in alarm, acknowledged
1 = Not in alarm, unacknowledged or reset required
2 = Low severity alarm, acknowledged
3 = Low severity alarm, unacknowledged
4 = Medium severity alarm, acknowledged
5 = Medium severity alarm, unacknowledged
6 = High severity alarm, acknowledged
7 = High severity alarm, unacknowledged
8 = Urgent severity alarm, acknowledged
9 = Urgent severity alarm, unacknowledged

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Separated Reset Reqd functions from Val_Notify  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(OnFail.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(OnFail.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(OffFail.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(OffFail.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(IOFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(IOFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,[XIC(OnFail.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(OffFail.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(IOFault.Val_Notify.0) ] OTE(Wrk_Notify.0) ,MOV(Wrk_Notify,Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="65" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung identifies:
* if a latched Shed condition requires a reset in order to run the motor;
* if that reset or any alarm reset or other reset is required; and
* if any reset or acknowledge from the operator is required.

#####  V3.0-04 2014-06-12: Fixed I/O Fault Ready to Reset logic.  #####
#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx); split from Val_Notify logic (above).  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(OnFail.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(OffFail.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(IOFault.Rdy_Ack) ] ,[XIC(OnFail.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(OffFail.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(IOFault.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(Nrdy_OperPrio) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) XIO(Sts_IOFault) ] OTE(Rdy_Reset) ]OTE(Rdy_ResetAckAll);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Prescan" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Clear Ownershp, clear "lurking" Commands, de-energize output]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PRESCAN (POWERUP) HANDLING
============================================================
On Prescan, set the Ownership to NO OWNER (0).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(PSet_Owner)CLR(Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTU(PCmd_On)OTU(PCmd_Off)OTU(PCmd_OnPulse)OTU(PCmd_OffPulse)OTU(PCmd_ContPulse);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_On) OTU(OCmd_Off) OTU(OCmd_OnPulse) OTU(OCmd_OffPulse) ,OTU(OCmd_ContPulse) OTU(OCmd_Bypass) OTU(OCmd_Check) OTU(MCmd_Disable) ,OTU(MCmd_Enable) OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Override Command is set to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the latched Shed faults.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Nrdy_OperPrio)OTU(Nrdy_Fail)OTU(Nrdy_IOFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Output is cleared on Prescan.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Out)OTU(Sts_Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Show the enumerated device command as NONE.
Show the enumerated device status as POWERUP / UNKNOWN
Show the enumerated internal state as DE-ENERGIZED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Val_Cmd)CLR(Val_Sts)CLR(Val_State);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_8"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_40"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_20"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_12"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_16"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="P_Alarm"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="P_Mode"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
